      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Came here to report this myself. My friend and I, both on desktop, were conversing casually but getting ratelimited, most likely due to the \"Send Text Automatically\" feature being enabled.\n\nI don't see why the chatbox ratelimits are so restrictive. They're also impairing to the use of chatbox (and possibly other?) OSC updates. The lack of transparency surrounding the ratelimit algorithm makes the functionality unpredictable and thus unreliable.\n\nI would prefer to be able to send chatbox updates at least twice a second, with some leeway/burst functionality also possible - without adding a cooldown unless further exceeded. It would be helpful at least for debugging purposes if there was some exposure via OSC of what ratelimits are in effect.\n\nAs another example, an application that provides heart rate data in the chatbox might also want to support the use of the chatbox for sending regular in-game messages - the ability to read the chatbox content would allow this.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
